\pard\fi-280\li400\sa80\f0\fs21 \bullet\tab config.py \u8212? added `weight_dependence: float = 0.0` after delta_minus, with a comment block explaining it. 0.0 = the shipped additive rule (byte-identical behaviour); 1.0 scales the LTD step by (w - w_min) and the LTP step by (w_max - w) \u8212? soft bounds. WHEN each happens is identical either way; this only sets magnitude. Note the config dataclass has a _StrictParams guard that rejects unknown attribute assignment.\par
\pard\fi-280\li400\sa80\f0\fs21 \bullet\tab sim/plasticity.py \u8212? the only functional model change. Added the weight_dependence parameter to __init__, self._w_span = w_max - w_min, a docstring paragraph on why the additive rule has no per-synapse fixed point, and the branch:\par
\pard\f1\fs17       wd = self.weight_dependence\par
\pard\f1\fs17       if wd == 0.0:\par
\pard\f1\fs17           weights[ltd_mask] -= self.delta_minus\par
\pard\f1\fs17           weights[ltp_mask] += self.delta_plus\par
\pard\f1\fs17       else:\par
\pard\f1\fs17           frac_down = (weights - self.w_min) / self._w_span\par
\pard\f1\fs17           frac_up   = (self.w_max - weights) / self._w_span\par
\pard\f1\fs17           weights[ltd_mask] -= self.delta_minus*((1.0-wd) + wd*frac_down[ltd_mask])\par
\pard\f1\fs17           weights[ltp_mask] += self.delta_plus *((1.0-wd) + wd*frac_up[ltp_mask])\par
\pard\fi-280\li400\sa80\f0\fs21 \bullet\tab sim/simulate.py \u8212? ONE line added: weight_dependence=cfg.weight_dependence, in the Plasticity(...) construction. The rest of that file's diff, plus sim/neurons.py, experiments/run_baseline.py and experiments/run_calibration.py, were PRE-EXISTING uncommitted changes from the earlier campaign. Verified. Not to be attributed to this work.\par
